ID(1)                          P32W Unix                           ID(1)

NAME
       id - print the user and group ids

SYNOPSIS
       id [-u | -g] [-n] [-r]

DESCRIPTION
       id prints the real user id and the real group id, each with
       its name from /etc/passwd or /etc/group (? if there is
       none). If the effective user id differs from the real one
       (a set-user-id program), it is added as euid=; likewise
       egid= for the group.

OPTIONS
       -u     print only the effective user id, as a number
       -g     print only the effective group id
       -n     with -u or -g: the name instead of the number (the
              number if there is no name)
       -r     with -u or -g: the real id instead of the effective

EXAMPLES
       $ id
       uid=100(ken) gid=10(staff)
       $ id -un
       ken

FILES
       /etc/passwd, /etc/group

EXIT STATUS
       0; 2 for a usage error (an unknown option, -u with -g, or
       -n or -r without either).

SEE ALSO
       whoami(1), who(1), su(1), passwd(5), group(5)

BUGS
       There is no -G and no user argument (id ken); supplementary
       groups are not shown.
